## Summary

Currently to get a true representative source document per each category, we need a 2 pass solution here which earlier could be achieved with a single DSL query

**DSL**  

```js  
{  
  aggs: {  
    sample: {  
      random_sampler: { probability: 0.1 },  
      aggs: {  
        categories: {  
          categorize_text: { field: 'message' },  
          aggs: {  
            top: { top_hits: { size: 1, fields: [{ field: '*', include_unmapped: true }] } }  
          }  
        }  
      }  
    }  
  }  
}  
```

One round trip → for each text category, one full document with **every field** in `hit.fields`.  

**ES|QL — pass 1 (categorize, pick representative)**  

```sql  
FROM <idx> METADATA _index, _id  
| EVAL doc_key = CONCAT(_index, ":", _id)  
| SAMPLE p  
| STATS representative_key = TOP(doc_key, 1, "desc"),  
        count = COUNT(*)  
  BY pattern = CATEGORIZE(<msg_field>)  
| SORT count DESC  
| LIMIT (size + offset)  
```  

**ES|QL — pass 2 (fetch full source for chosen ids)**  

```sql  
FROM <idx> METADATA _index, _id, _source  
| EVAL doc_key = CONCAT(_index, ":", _id)  
| WHERE doc_key IN (<keys from pass 1>)  
| KEEP _index, _id, _source  
| LIMIT <docKeys.length>  
```

**Why two passes**

`TOP`, `SAMPLE(field, n)`, `VALUES`, `FIRST` operate on a single field per group. Chaining `SAMPLE(message, 1), SAMPLE(log.level, 1), …` does **not** guarantee the sampled values come from the same document — coherence is lost. There is no single ES|QL aggregation in 9.4 that materializes a coherent `_source` per group.

