When a field has `multi_value: false, on_failure: ignore` and receives a duplicate value, `FieldMapper.parse()` sets `redirectedToFailureColumn = true` and skips `parseCreateField` — correctly rejecting the duplicate from the parent. However, `doParseMultiFields` runs unconditionally, so the multi-field still indexes the rejected value.

Today's broken behavior: given `field` (keyword, `multi_value: false, on_failure: ignore`) with a `field.raw` multi-field, indexing `["first", "second"]` produces:
- `field` → `["first"]` (duplicate rejected)
- `field.raw` → `["first", "second"]` (duplicate indexed anyway)

Parent and multi-field are no longer aligned. This can cause search inconsistencies where a multi-field matches a query but the parent does not include the matching value.

## Fix

Gate `doParseMultiFields` on `redirectedToFailureColumn == false`, mirroring the existing gate on `parseCreateField` in `FieldMapper.java`.

## Approach (per Salvatore's suggestion)

1. Add a suite of tests that verify parent and multi-field always hold the same values. Something like:

```java
public void testMultiFieldsSkippedForViolationRejectedDuplicate() throws Exception {
    DocumentMapper mapper = createMapperService(mapping(b -> {
        b.startObject("field");
        b.field("type", "keyword");
        b.field("multi_value", false);
        b.field("on_failure", "ignore");
        b.startObject("fields");
        b.startObject("raw").field("type", "keyword").endObject();
        b.endObject();
        b.endObject();
    })).documentMapper();

    ParsedDocument doc = mapper.parse(source(b -> b.array("field", "first", "second")));

    assertThat(doc.rootDoc().getValues("field"), arrayContaining("first"));
    assertThat(doc.rootDoc().getValues("field.raw"), arrayContaining("first")); // fails today
}
```

2. Some tests will fail, confirming the inconsistency.
3. Apply the fix (`redirectedToFailureColumn` gate on `doParseMultiFields`) and confirm all tests pass.

## Location

`FieldMapper.parse()` — `server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/FieldMapper.java`

